  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Since we need to multiply $\\frac{11}{12}$ by $2$, we repeat the fraction model $2$ times, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14129810/assets/e8c59fe9adfedd533dcefb93fc62c9d9e911d63f8140a656537143ff2f8f2ae3.png)\n\n \n\nThere are $11\\times 2=22$ shaded pieces in total. Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\frac{11}{12}\\times 2=\\frac{22}{12}.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
